From a4421e19a4e16cb6e827a17f9445d8d5bf8a7f69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:10:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add palmLegacyManager: serve the Palm-era com.palm.audio
 API

LuneOS' UI is Enyo 1.0. com.palm.app.phone drives calls through TIL and
expects audio control on com.palm.audio/phone, /ringtone, /dtmf and
/telephony; the enyo framework plays UI feedback through
com.palm.audio/systemsounds; the music player uses /media. None of that
exists in this generation of audiod -- the scenario modules that provided
it were dropped when audiod-pro was restructured around audioPolicyManager,
and AUDIOD_PALM_LEGACY now survives only in CMakeLists.txt.

Rather than restore the whole scenario engine, this module reimplements the
calls LuneOS actually makes and maps them onto current audiod internals. It
also serves org.webosports.service.audio, so luna-sysmgr's DisplayManager
and the Settings app keep working once audio-service is retired.

LS2 gives a handle exactly one name, so the two legacy names get their own
handles here; audiod's own com.webos.service.audio is untouched.

Two routing bugs found by decompiling the webOS 3.0.5 audiod are fixed by
construction rather than carried forward:

* The disconnect path there reset the call mode without pushing it to the
  device, so the device-side cache stayed on the finished call and the next
  call's identical mode hit an early return, skipping the route switch
  entirely. Here the applied mode is tracked next to the requested one and
  the disconnect transition always applies.

* A scenario change arriving before the call went Active was dropped
  outright. setCurrentScenario now applies whenever a call mode is set, and
  updateCallMode() picks the route up on the Active transition otherwise.

DTMF tone synthesis is not ported yet: the methods reply success so the
dialpad does not see bus errors, but stay silent. applyCallRouting() is the
seam where the card-profile switching lands.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific legacy API]
